  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nIssue #980 part 2: the user's STEP bore (`testdata/models/Milling-test.step`) gets its HSM Adaptive plan back on every level - Z 10 (lost since #839) and Z 20 (lost since #850).\r\n\r\n**Cause (measured, not guessed).** The Z 10 level's center area and plan were dumped from the heavy test on main. The plan is one star-morph walk; its \"crossing\" at (-1.99, -0.13) is segment 0 (the entry orbit's first chord, out of the start point) against segment 96 (the spiral's first chord, out of the orbit's closing vertex). `adaptive::rings::circle` computed the closing vertex at `a0 + TAU`, 7.7e-16 mm off the start, and the plan's crossing law (orientation predicate) read that ulp as a proper crossing. The Z 20 fallback is the same seam (segments 0 and 96, endpoints 8.9e-16 apart). Which level the float noise hit was luck of the outline - #839's finer mesh only reshuffled it; no near-duplicate vertex, sliver or arc-fit defect is involved.\r\n\r\n**Fix** (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/rings.rs`, `circle`): the circle closes exactly - its last point is its first, and where the start lies on the circle (within `ON_CIRCLE` = 1e-9 mm) both are the start itself. The snap moves a point by at most 1e-9 mm, six orders under the 0.005 mm verify tolerance. The crossing law (`adaptive::guard`) is unchanged: a plan that really crosses itself still falls back to rings by name.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\nHeavy pin `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` (release, `--ignored`), three runs, identical: no level falls back (`fell` empty), no warnings (verifies clean against the part solid), no budget refusal; 16197 moves / 15458 planar feeds / 1581 arcs (was 6500 / 6464 / 222 with Z 20 and Z 10 on rings; 5530 / 5497 / 600 before #839). Z 20 is back on its HSM plan with 58 microlift returns, hence far more moves than its rings.\r\n\r\nThe reviewer's open point from PR #1003 (does a rings level clear its stock as fully as the HSM plan?) is moot for this part: no level of the bore falls back now.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n- `crates/motion/tests/adaptive_orbit_seam.rs::the_users_z10_bore_level_keeps_its_hsm_plan` (new, debug ~7 s): the dumped Z 10 center outline (287 vertices, `crates/motion/tests/fixtures/bore_z10_center.txt`) grown back by the tool radius into a 2-D pocket. Before the fix: \"crosses itself at (-2.09, -0.13) ... Offset rings cut this pocket instead\"; after: the HSM plan stands, with arcs.\r\n- `machining2d::adaptive::rings::tests::the_orbit_closes_on_its_own_start_and_the_spiral_leaves_it_uncrossed` (new unit pin): 400 orbit seeds; the orbit closes on its start and a spiral leaving it is no crossing (before the fix most seeds crossed, the first at the Z 10 point exactly).\r\n- Heavy pin re-measured (above), three release runs.\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green (motion suites 359 s, app pocket3d_hsm build-only; log quick-20261112-032535). `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --tests`: green. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- Motion heavy lanes touching adaptive (release, `--ignored`): `-- --ignored adaptive` (2 tests) and the whole ignored sets of adaptive_hsm (5), adaptive_band, pocket3d_hsm (1), rotary_adaptive (3), trochoid_slot: all green, none moved. No golden changed.\r\n\r\n## Heavy pin per platform (review round)\r\n\r\nThe contributor's reviewer measured this head on macOS Apple silicon: 16160 / 15432 / 1571, against Windows x86_64's 16197 / 15458 / 1581 (the planner is not bit-stable across platforms - issue #1010). The `(moves, planar, arcs)` triple is now exact per measured platform via `cfg` (Windows x86_64, macOS aarch64), and a band (moves 16100..=16260, planar 15380..=15520, arcs 1560..=1600) on any unmeasured target, with a comment asking for its exact triple. No warnings, no fallback level and no budget note stay exact everywhere. Re-run on f9a9ba87: heavy pin (release) 16197 / 15458 / 1581, pass; `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` clean.\r\n\r\nRelation to fork PR #1014: it rewrites the same assertions for the old plan (Z 20 + Z 10 on rings, 6500 / 6464 / 222) as ranges. Once this merges those numbers are gone; #1014 should take this per-platform form with its own measured triple (only if its platform is not already covered), or close.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\nOther heavy lanes outside the motion adaptive suites and the app bore pin; the GUI.\r\n\r\nDecision: `docs/decisions/980-bore-hsm-plan.md`.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Adaptive (HSM) roughing no longer drops a level to Offset rings as \"crosses itself\" because the entry orbit's closing point sat a rounding error off its start - the user's STEP bore keeps the HSM plan on every level (#980)\r\n\r\nEffort: high (no escalation)\r\n\r\nFixes #980\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
